From f1848c45dc7d00357e488d1f9206f0e26b572a1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:35:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): hidden preview opens wait for a ready guest and
 host other profiles off view [daveey]

preview.open acknowledged as soon as the pane registered its script runner,
which happens before Electron attaches the guest; the next read/act could
throw 'preview webview is not ready'. The pane now publishes the guest's
lifecycle (loading / dom-ready / main-frame failure) and the open waits for a
fresh dom-ready for the page it asked for, or fails with the load error.

A hidden chat of a profile not in view used to be refused. Its tab now joins
its own profile's bucket and mounts parked off view ($offViewPreviewTabs):
the viewed profile's rail, drawer and pins never see it, its owner's
read/act reach it, and focusing that chat later shows the same guest.

Born-parked hosts get a 1280x800 kept size: a 0x0 guest has a 0x0 viewport
where trusted input never lands (verified in an isolated Electron run).
---
